<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.13.1: Equivalent Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01967</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.13.1: Equivalent Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a562cede-827b-460c-be52-604fe59e6103</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
  <item>Complete each row with an equivalent expression in standard form or factored form.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable" id="table-00001">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry></row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00001">\(x^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00002">a. _____</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00003">d. _____</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00004">\(x(x+9)\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00005">\(x^2-18x\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00006">b. _____</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00007">e. _____</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00008">\(x(6-x)\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00009">\(-x^2+10x\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00010">c. _____</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00011">f. _____</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para id="para-00012">\(-x(x+2.75)\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<example id="exam-00001"><exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    
    <para id="para-00013"> What is the factored form of \(x^2\)? </para>
      <para id="para-00014">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
  <para id="para-00015">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00016">\(x\cdot x\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example id="exam-00002"><exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    
    <para id="para-00017"> What is the factored form of \(x^2-18x\)? </para>
      <para id="para-00018">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
  <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00020"> \(x(x-18)\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example id="exam-00003"><exercise id="exer-00003">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    
    <para id="para-00021"> What is the factored form of \(-x^2+10x\)? </para>
      <para id="para-00022">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
  <para id="para-00023">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00024">\(-x(x-10)\) or \(x(-x+10)\) or \(x(10-x)\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example id="exam-00004"><exercise id="exer-00004">
  <problem id="prob-00004">
    
    <para id="para-00025"> What is the standard form of \(x(x+9)\)? </para>
      <para id="para-00026">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00004">
  <para id="para-00027">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00028">\(x^2+9x\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example id="exam-00005"><exercise id="exer-00005">
  <problem id="prob-00005">
    
    <para id="para-00029"> What is the standard form of \(x(6-x)\)? </para>
      <para id="para-00030">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00005">
  <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00032">\(-x^2+6x\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example id="exam-00006"><exercise id="exer-00006">
  <problem id="prob-00006">
    
    <para id="para-00033"> What is the standard form of \(-x(x+2.75)\)? </para>
      <para id="para-00034">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00006">
  <para id="para-00035">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00036">\(-x^2-2.75x\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00007">
  <problem id="prob-00007">
    <para id="para-00037"> What do the quadratic expressions in each column have in common (besides the fact that everything in the left column is in standard form and everything in the other column is in factored form)? Be prepared to share your observations. </para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00007">
    
    <para id="para-00038">Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00039">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00040"> In the left column, all the expressions in standard form have a squared term and a linear term but no constant term, and the squared term has a coefficient of either 1 or -1. In the right column, one of the factors is just a variable whose coefficient is 1 or -1, and the other factor is either a sum or a difference.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
</document>